  "id": "COMPOUND:38172 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Bezerramycin B is implicated in targeting the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is known to regulate gene expression by methylating histone H3 lysine 27. This complex is involved in various cellular processes, including cell proliferation and differentiation, and its dysregulation has been linked to several diseases. The evidence suggests that Bezerramycin B acts as a target for multiple compounds, including (2S,9R,11S,13R,14S,15S,17S)-11,14,15-trihydroxy-4-methoxy-2,6,14,17-tetramethyl-10-oxatetracyclo[7.7.1.02,7.013,17]heptadec-4-ene-3,16-dione and (2S,4R)-4-Hydroxyglutamic Acid, which in turn target FaDu. These compounds are likely to exert their effects through the same mechanism, influencing the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex and thereby modulating the activity of the PRC2 complex in FaDu cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Bezerramycin B in regulating gene expression through the PRC2 complex, which may have implications for cellular processes in FaDu cells.",
